77,220,400,16,15,4130,10,16,19,87,10,16,20,88,28,16,21,21,12947,220,7379,400,87,43010,12947,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nFor $(x,y)$, positive integers, let  $10xy+14x+15y=166$.  Find $x+y$.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"bf08c7bbb66bba0036b0d4e8cada229ebca72714d1a210597497fc154addc258"},"seconds":56.8805615901947,"seed":31048668006465614,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the equation \\(10xy + 14x + 15y = 166\\) for positive integers \\(x\\) and \\(y\\), we will first try to transform the equation into a form that might allow us to factor it.\n\n1. **Add and Subtract a Term to Factor:**\n   We start by adding and subtracting a term to the equation to facilitate factoring. Notice that adding and subtracting 21 (which is the product of the coefficients of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) divided by the coefficient of \\(xy\\)) can help:\n   \\[\n   10xy + 14x + 15y + 21 - 21 = 166\n   \\]\n   This can be rewritten as:\n   \\[\n   10xy + 14x + 15y + 21 = 187\n   \\]\n\n2. **Factor the Left-Hand Side:**\n   The left-hand side can now be factored by grouping:\n   \\[\n   (10x + 15)(y + \\frac{14}{10}) = 187\n   \\]\n   Simplifying the fraction inside the parentheses:\n   \\[\n   (10x + 15)(y + 1.4) = 187\n   \\]\n   To avoid dealing with decimals, we can multiply everything by 10:\n   \\[\n   (10x + 15)(10y + 14) = 1870\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find Factor Pairs of 1870:**\n   We need to find pairs of factors of 1870 that fit the form \\((10x + 15)\\) and \\((10y + 14)\\). First, list the factor pairs of 1870:\n   \\[\n   1870 = 2 \\times 935, \\quad 1870 = 5 \\times 374, \\quad 1870 = 10 \\times 187, \\quad 1870 = 11 \\times 170, \\quad 1870 = 17 \\times 110, \\quad 1870 = 22 \\times 85, \\quad 1870 = 34 \\times 55\n   \\]\n\n4. **Test Each Pair:**\n   We test each factor pair to see if they fit the form \\((10x + 15)\\) and \\((10y + 14)\\):\n   - For \\(10x + 15 = 34\\) and \\(10y + 14 = 55\\):\n     \\[\n     10x + 15 = 34 \\implies 10x = 19 \\implies x = 1.9 \\quad (\\text{not an integer})\n     \\]\n   - For \\(10x + 15 = 55\\) and \\(10y + 14 = 34\\):\n     \\[\n     10x + 15 = 55 \\implies 10x = 40 \\implies x = 4\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     10y + 14 = 34 \\implies 10y = 20 \\implies y = 2\n     \\]\n     Both \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) are integers, so this pair works.\n\n5. **Verify the Solution:**\n   Substitute \\(x = 4\\) and \\(y = 2\\) back into the original equation:\n   \\[\n   10(4)(2) + 14(4) + 15(2) = 80 + 56 + 30 = 166\n   \\]\n   The solution satisfies the original equation.\n\n6. **Calculate \\(x + y\\):**\n   \\[\n   x + y = 4 + 2 = 6\n   \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{6}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
